<title>JAPAN: Mori Denki sets terms of convertible bond.</title>
<headline>Mori Denki sets terms of convertible bond.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>BORROWER - Mori Denki Manufacturing Co Ltd</p>
<p>LEAD MGR</p>
<p> TYPE Eurodollar convertible  ISSUE NO	   AMT   15 million dollars</p>
<p> COUPON	4.0 pct    ISS PRICE  par	MATURITY 6.Jan.01</p>
<p> CONV PRICE  416 yen    CURR RATE 1 dollar/113.5 yen</p>
<p> CONV FROM   1.Feb.97   CONV TO   27.Dec.01</p>
<p> LAST MOODY'S	     PAY DATE 10.Jan.97  INT PAY</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P		   SIGN DATE	     SUB DATE</p>
<p> LAST JCR		   LAST JBRI	     LAST NIS</p>
<p>NOTE: Conversion price will be either 416 yen or the closing price of Mori Denki's stock price on the Tokyo Stock Exchange prior to conversion.</p>
</text>
